{{Quote|The Moff has a light cruiser. It could be helpful in your effort to regain Mandalore.|Din Djarin, to Bo-Katan Kryze, regarding Gideon's Class 546 Cruiser|<ref name="Chapter 16" />}}
'''Gideon's light cruiser'''<ref name="Chapter 12" /> was a [[Class 546 Cruiser|Class 546 model]]<ref name="Chapter 15" /> of the [[Arquitens-class command cruiser|''Arquitens''-class command cruiser]]<ref name="Battles that Changed the Galaxy" /> under the command of [[Moff]] [[Gideon]] in the [[Standard year|years]] after the [[Battle of Endor]].<ref name="Chapter 12" /> During the [[Second rescue of Grogu|rescue]] of his [[foundling]], [[Din Grogu|Grogu]], from Gideon, the [[Mandalorian]] [[Din Djarin]] and his allies seized the [[Starship|ship]] and captured the moff. The [[light cruiser]] also contained a [[platoon]] of [[Phase-III Dark Trooper]]s, though they were destroyed by Djarin and [[Jedi Master]] [[Luke Skywalker]].<ref name="Chapter 16" /> Control of the cruiser was then handed over to [[Bo-Katan Kryze]].<ref name="ACPOV" /> When Kryze's forces left her after she did not take the Darksaber from Din Djarin, command of the vessel fell to [[Axe Woves]], who used it for mercenary work and later as a flagship for the [[Mandalorian fleet]]. The vessel was eventually destroyed during the [[Liberation of Mandalore]], when Woves steered the vessel onto a collision course with Gideon's [[Mandalore Imperial base|Imperial base]], killing the Moff and his remaining forces.<ref name="Chapter 24>{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 24: The Return}}</ref>

==Description==
The [[Arquitens-class command cruiser|''Arquitens''-class command cruiser]] was the mobile headquarters of the moff,<ref name="Chapter 16" /> and when it was taken by the Mandalorians, it had the symbol of the [[mythosaur]] on its underbelly,<ref name="Chapter 22" /> similar to the [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo|Thrawn's]] flagship, the [[Imperial I-class Star Destroyer|''Imperial I''-class Star Destroyer]] ''[[Chimaera]],'' with the [[Chimaera (symbol)|symbol]] of the [[Chimaera (creature)|chimaera]] on its underbelly.<ref name="Iron Squadron">{{Rebels|Iron Squadron (episode)}}</ref>

{{Ship-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The light cruiser first appeared in "[[Chapter 12: The Siege]]," an episode of the live-action TV show ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'', which aired in [[2020]].<ref name="Chapter 12" /> It was realized by the building of a detailed five-foot scale model.<ref name="Gallery">{{DisneyGallery|Disney Gallery: The Mandalorian: Making of Season Two|Making of Season Two}}</ref>

